{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482563-sculpting-and-enchanting-gargoyles-and-statues","id":1482563,"title":"Sculpting and Enchanting Gargoyles and Statues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-31T19:32:12-07:00","id":1482563,"title":"Sculpting and Enchanting Gargoyles and Statues","content":"Would sculping be Dexterity + Crafts or Intelligence + Crafts?<br /> <br /> With Sphere Ranks 3 or less, what self-targeted spell would best improve the Mage Sculptor's creation process?<br /> <br /> What kind of physical properties would it be fun for a statue to have?<br /> <br /> What kind of Enchantments would you put on it? <br /> <br /> Would you keep it or display it in a public place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T20:40:58-07:00","id":1482570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482563-sculpting-and-enchanting-gargoyles-and-statues#post1482563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Sphere Ranks 3 or less, what self-targeted spell would best improve the Mage Sculptor's creation process?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind 1 and Entropy 2 are always your best friends when trying to simply &quot;get better&quot; at a skill roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What kind of physical properties would it be fun for a statue to have? </div> </div> </div>What do you mean? <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . What kind of Enchantments would you put on it? </div> </div> </div>That depends on the Spheres I myself have. If I had Mind 5 for example I'd give it intelligence, but with slave mentalith","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T15:07:11-07:00","id":1482666,"title":"","content":"I would personally make sculpting Intelligence + Crafts, but improving the roll wouldn't require a lot by itself.<br /> <br /> For properties, I think being able to change colors to blend with local statuary, masonry or columns would be nice. Blend with stone and masonry would also be interesting, even if just superficially to become a part of the fixture without breaking it. And vibration-based senses, so their human-ish appearance doesn't actually give any clue about their sensory abilities and dependencies.<br /> <br /> While gargoyles are always a classic, I have a particular falling for caryatid columns, and enchantments to let them leave their places without causing structural damage to the location is important. Also Mind effects to either make them inconspicuous (people do not feel strange to have a statue or column there, maybe even half-remember some possible explanation), make people ignore objects they carry (they can appreciate the statue, but whatever it takes or carries that isn't stone becomes invisible or look like a part of the statue), and/or improve the feelings the work itself causes (whatever it is, just increases their artistic impact as taken by the observer).<br /> <br /> You could have an easier time just making the statue invisible with Forces, but I think it kind of defeats the whole idea of using a statue in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T16:44:16-07:00","id":1482680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482563-sculpting-and-enchanting-gargoyles-and-statues?p=1482570#post1482570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 1 and Entropy 2 are always your best friends when trying to simply &quot;get better&quot; at a skill roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I'm creating NPCs and determining what spheres they would need for the projects they are involved in, I almost feel obligated to to give them all Mind 1, just for the multitasking and memory. There is certainly an Entropic luck element if you are working with materials that can chip in unintended ways under your chisel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482563-sculpting-and-enchanting-gargoyles-and-statues?p=1482570#post1482570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, well, see the answer by <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482563-sculpting-and-enchanting-gargoyles-and-statues?p=1482570#post1482570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends on the Spheres I myself have. If I had Mind 5 for example I'd give it intelligence, but with slave mentalith</div> </div> </div> </div>Planescape: Torment has a statue with quest-essential information who you need to assist in gaining back some freedom. It's a fun errand. I could see a kind of justification for making the statue a slave, if its independent travels would invite paradox or resonance tracing by foes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482563-sculpting-and-enchanting-gargoyles-and-statues?p=1482666#post1482666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI would personally make sculpting Intelligence + Crafts, but improving the roll wouldn't require a lot by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind 1 <i>really is</i> your best friend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482563-sculpting-and-enchanting-gargoyles-and-statues?p=1482666#post1482666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For properties, I think being able to change colors to blend with local statuary, masonry or columns would be nice. Blend with stone and masonry would also be interesting, even if just superficially to become a part of the fixture without breaking it. And vibration-based senses, so their human-ish appearance doesn't actually give any clue about their sensory abilities and dependencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be totally coincidental ground penetrating (and conventional) radar or simple motion detection. For a mystical statue, I would just say that the components could be added, pre-enchanting, made to function once and then melted into the rest of the interior material during the enchanting process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482563-sculpting-and-enchanting-gargoyles-and-statues?p=1482666#post1482666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While gargoyles are always a classic, I have a particular falling for caryatid columns, and enchantments to let them leave their places without causing structural damage to the location is important. Also Mind effects to either make them inconspicuous (people do not feel strange to have a statue or column there, maybe even half-remember some possible explanation), make people ignore objects they carry (they can appreciate the statue, but whatever it takes or carries that isn't stone becomes invisible or look like a part of the statue), and/or improve the feelings the work itself causes (whatever it is, just increases their artistic impact as taken by the observer).</div> </div> </div> </div>On caryatid columns, I thought back to a D&amp;D campaign I ran with a Succubus and a Bard as plot background characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482563-sculpting-and-enchanting-gargoyles-and-statues?p=1482666#post1482666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have an easier time just making the statue invisible with Forces, but I think it kind of defeats the whole idea of using a statue in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking, since it's in a witch's garden, it could absorb sunlight during the day and shine at night to maximize the yield of the garden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T17:32:11-07:00","id":1482686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482563-sculpting-and-enchanting-gargoyles-and-statues?p=1482680#post1482680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I'm creating NPCs and determining what spheres they would need for the projects they are involved in, I almost feel obligated to to give them all Mind 1, just for the multitasking and memory. There is certainly an Entropic luck element if you are working with materials that can chip in unintended ways under your chisel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entropy 2 does a lot more than just that. It can help you create the Leonardo Da Vinci of the Gargoyles with a bunch of successes stored.<br /> <br /> What effects to give... It's very limitless actually, I would need to know the Spheres you have. Forces 3 (I would argue 2) with Matter 3 to allow it to move by itself. Then, you would need to either awaken it's own spirit to allow it independency without you needing to control it as a puppet all the time (probably the best method), or you invite another spirit to inhabit it (which may have some unforseeable consequences) or use Mind 5 to say &quot;Parla&quot;, but that is obviously the most expensive option in terms of necessary power (a 5 Sphere is no joke). After &quot;giving life&quot; to it... You can do whatever. Turn it into a &quot;not-exactly&quot; &quot;living&quot; Wonder with Prime, using Prime to place a bunch of cool stuff and link all that with its mind so the statue can &quot;cast&quot; all those &quot;spells&quot; by itself.<br /> <br /> If you have Life 6 and Matter 6 (you know, the basics of every noob), turn it into a new breedable &quot;species&quot;... Who are already born with all those &quot;magic spells&quot; (using Prime 6 probably? Yeah, easy stuff). That would be something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T18:12:07-07:00","id":1482691,"title":"","content":"<span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, I'm thinking that the sculptor and enchanter are two different people, the hired sculptor having spheres 3 or under. The owner of the property, Alice, has: Prime 3, Forces 2, Matter 2, Life 4, Mind 3, Correspondence 3, Time 3, Entropy 2. She belongs to a Chantry, the membership of which have quite a bit of sphere coverage with quite a few rank 4s. Prisha, who lives within a twenty minute drive has Entropy 3, Time 3, Mind 3, Spirit 3, the last of which she could use to contact friendly spirits with the offer of a statue to inhabit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T06:41:07-07:00","id":1482738,"title":"","content":"Well, Forces 2 Matter 3 is enough to allow the statue to move around as if alive. Since Alice doesnt have Matter 3, only Forces 2, she can enchant the statue to move as a solid block, as a big rock.<br /> <br /> With Mind 3 she can connect the movement with the statue's &quot;mind&quot;. If some other member of her Cabal has Matter 3, Mind 3 and Forces 2, creating the self moving statue would be a big favor.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;intellect&quot; of it, it can be replaced by a spirit obviously, since Mind 5 aint that easy to find. Spirit 2 is enough to summon, and after a while and a lot of perseverance, eventually you'll find a spirit willing and capable of inhabiting the statue by its own. To place UNCAPABLE spirits however, but who would otherwise be more suitable and more cooperative, you would need Spirit 4, that way you're not dependant on the spirit having the power to do it, and such spirit would be much more grateful, since it's only by your own grace that it is allowed such an opportunity.<br /> <br /> Not of that is necessary thou, because with Spirit 3 you can simply awaken the Spirit of the Gargoyle itself, and let the statue decide by itself. The advantage here is that the gargoyle would most likely be fiercily loyal; Prisha, who has Spirit 3, would after all be her &quot;mother&quot;. Unless treated as a mindless slave, such spirit would probably have undying loyalty, going beyond the &quot;line of duty&quot;.<br /> <br /> The best part is, the effect for making the statue move by itself (Mind 3, Forces 2, Matter 3) doesnt need to be made togheter with the one to awaken the spirit of it, therefore they can be done by different Mages.<br /> <br /> Of course, all these effects have to be permanent.<br /> <br /> Now that this is settled, let us see what else can be done to give some cool upgrades to this little thing...<br /> <br /> Well, Mind 2 can be used to give it &quot;Terror&quot;, an aura of fear. <br /> <br /> Let Prisha use Entropy 3 to make it extra durable.<br /> <br /> Matter 2 can &quot;regenerate&quot; it as needed.<br /> <br /> There's more obviously, but I have to think about it, the reason being that I know all Sphere's levels by memory, but only from third edition. I need to check M20 to see in detail all the modifications in order not to pass some outdated information","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T09:34:05-07:00","id":1482779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482563-sculpting-and-enchanting-gargoyles-and-statues?p=1482738#post1482738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Forces 2 Matter 3 is enough to allow the statue to move around as if alive. Since Alice doesnt have Matter 3, only Forces 2, she can enchant the statue to move as a solid block, as a big rock.<br /> <br /> With Mind 3 she can connect the movement with the statue's &quot;mind&quot;. If some other member of her Cabal has Matter 3, Mind 3 and Forces 2, creating the self moving statue would be a big favor.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;intellect&quot; of it, it can be replaced by a spirit obviously, since Mind 5 aint that easy to find. Spirit 2 is enough to summon, and after a while and a lot of perseverance, eventually you'll find a spirit willing and capable of inhabiting the statue by its own. To place UNCAPABLE spirits however, but who would otherwise be more suitable and more cooperative, you would need Spirit 4, that way you're not dependant on the spirit having the power to do it, and such spirit would be much more grateful, since it's only by your own grace that it is allowed such an opportunity.<br /> <br /> Not of that is necessary thou, because with Spirit 3 you can simply awaken the Spirit of the Gargoyle itself, and let the statue decide by itself. The advantage here is that the gargoyle would most likely be fiercily loyal; Prisha, who has Spirit 3, would after all be her &quot;mother&quot;. Unless treated as a mindless slave, such spirit would probably have undying loyalty, going beyond the &quot;line of duty&quot;.<br /> <br /> The best part is, the effect for making the statue move by itself (Mind 3, Forces 2, Matter 3) doesnt need to be made togheter with the one to awaken the spirit of it, therefore they can be done by different Mages.<br /> <br /> Of course, all these effects have to be permanent.<br /> <br /> Now that this is settled, let us see what else can be done to give some cool upgrades to this little thing...<br /> <br /> Well, Mind 2 can be used to give it &quot;Terror&quot;, an aura of fear.<br /> <br /> Let Prisha use Entropy 3 to make it extra durable.<br /> <br /> Matter 2 can &quot;regenerate&quot; it as needed.<br /> <br /> There's more obviously, but I have to think about it, the reason being that I know all Sphere's levels by memory, but only from third edition. I need to check M20 to see in detail all the modifications in order not to pass some outdated information</div> </div> </div> </div>Some good ideas. One player made a character stranded in our timeline who is from an Everett Volume where there are fully functional androids. Statues that walk and talk are appropriate to the game. A Gaian Spirit fits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}